{"title":"Career Roadmap · Archaeology Assistant","role":"Archaeology Assistant","summary":"An Archaeology Assistant supports archaeologists, museums, universities, heritage organisations and cultural institutions with field surveys, excavation documentation, artefact recording, photography, GIS mapping, archival research, conservation support and archaeological data management.","facts":{"Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts - General / Honours)","Course":"Ancient Indian History, Culture & Archaeology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["highly practical and combines archaeology","history","fieldwork","documentation","GIS","heritage technology."],"sep":"+","label":"The role is"},{"type":"p","text":"Typical route:"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA Ancient Indian History, Culture & Archaeology","Field/Heritage Internship","Archaeology Assistant","Field Archaeologist / Research Assistant","Archaeologist / Heritage Specialist","Project Lead / Senior Archaeologist"]},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"An assistant-level role may accept an undergraduate background depending on the employer, while many professional archaeologist, specialist, research and government positions require postgraduate qualifications and/or specific subject eligibility. Always verify the current recruitment notification."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Stage","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2027"},{"text":"Foundation"},{"text":"Indian history + archaeology fundamentals"}],[{"text":"2027–2028"},{"text":"Skill Building"},{"text":"Field methods + documentation"}],[{"text":"2028–2029"},{"text":"Specialisation"},{"text":"GIS + archaeological research"}],[{"text":"2029–2031"},{"text":"Entry"},{"text":"Archaeology Assistant / Field Assistant"}],[{"text":"2031–2034"},{"text":"Development"},{"text":"Archaeological Research Assistant / Fi